From 9818e1166a108a576c480f9e76fa58430627a02e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mahyar (Mac) McDonald" <22130+theontho@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:08:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Phase ONT and PacBio reads and calls as upstream does
 (wgsextract #739)

With --phase_reads (the ONT_R104 and PacBio models), the port's
make_examples phased reads with DirectPhasing only for the small model's
features, and differed from upstream's make_examples_core.py elsewhere:

- It never wrote the phases into the reads' HP tags, so the pileups were
  not sorted by haplotype and their haplotype channel was 0.
- DirectPhasing read the padded region again from the BAM, without the
  partition's read cap, instead of phasing the partition's own reads. Now,
  as upstream, alleles are counted over the region padded by 20% (each
  side) from the reads overlapping the region, DirectPhasing phases those
  reads with every candidate of the padded region, their HP tags are
  replaced with the phases (dropped when phasing is skipped above 5,000
  candidates), and the candidates are cut back to the region. Regions
  without candidates are phased (and recorded) too.
- MakeExamplesOptions.realigner_options was empty unless reads were
  realigned, so the alt-aligned pileups (diff_channels) aligned reads to
  each alt haplotype with all-zero scores. It now holds the realigner
  flags' options, as upstream's does.
- --output_phase_info adds ALT_PS, PS_CONTIG and FIRST_VARIANT_IN_BLOCK to
  each candidate (upstream's add_phasing_to_candidate), which the fuzzy
  read-support channel (ONT) uses, and the small model tags a candidate
  MID=small_model as upstream's does. The port's own per-region PS and
  is_phased on big-model candidates, which upstream doesn't set, are gone.
- --output_local_read_phasing writes each phased read's phase by region
  (regions numbered in reference order across tasks); a failed write fails
  the stage.

postprocess_variants phases genotypes from ALT_PS (upstream's
maybe_phase_genotype) and, with --phased_reads_input_path, merges the
regions' read phases (upstream's merge_phased_reads, now built) and stitches
phase sets across regions (postprocess_variants.cc's StitchPhaseSets),
writing PS where upstream's records have it. The merge runs before the calls
are read, and an unreadable shard or switches file fails the stage rather
than treating regions as matching. Calls without ALT_PS (the trio path's
own phasing) keep their phase. run passes these flags for the
PACBIO and ONT models, as run_deepvariant does.

On a 1 Mb HG002 ONT R10.4.1 slice the examples (images and variant protos),
the small model's calls (probabilities within 2.4e-6), the read phases and
the VCF's sites, phased genotypes, filters and phase sets match
google/deepvariant:1.10.0's.
